+// BATCH ENTRY POINTS (spike-batch-ops-neon). The rows named fix*Batch* time the array APIs:
+// BATCH mode calls the API once per pass over 4096 lanes (SoA arrays, or AoS fixVec3 arrays
+// for the *AoS* rows), so the gate scan is inside the timed region; a tree without the API
+// runs the scalar function over the same arrays, which is the "before" column. SCALAR mode
+// is the generic dependent chain over the row's apply, which is a FOUR-lane call per step;
+// the fed-back word is shifted into the int30 range so the chain stays on the gated path.
+static fixed_t opBatchA[6][OP_BENCH_BATCH];
+static fixed_t opBatchOut[3][OP_BENCH_BATCH];
+static fixVec3 opBatchVa[OP_BENCH_BATCH];
